                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Its not often I say to not give a game a shot. My previous game reviews say as much. There's always something to enjoy. This game however feels like it wasn't meant to be played. Every ghost interaction is just \"Run until it gets tired\" and \"Just loop the rooms\" but the game doesn't really explain that. It feels like its setting up something interesting with locking the coffin to seal away the first ghost but it doesn't return to that. Or maybe it does because upon discovering how you are supposed top find the secret basement, I quit. I went to the alcove behind the stairs way earlier, it had already mentions secret passages, I just didn't go there when the game wanted so as far as it was concerned, it did not in fact exist. The audio also glitched out half way which showed that without proper sound design this game wasn't scary in the slightest. Its free so you aren't losing much but don't go in hoping for a good time.",
